# AGENT.md — src/adapters/

The "outside" layer. Everything here depends on `core/` — never the reverse.

## What lives here

- `controllers/` — Koa ctx handlers. Controllers receive use-cases through
  their constructor. Errors thrown in controller methods are caught by the
  top-level error middleware — no try/catch needed.
- `routes/` — factories that take a pre-wired controller and return a
  Koa `Router`. The wiring (`new Controller(...)`) happens in `app.ts`.
- `presenters/` — maps domain entities to views (API response shapes).
  Changing the response format should touch this file and nothing in `core/`.
- `dto/` — request body shapes and validation schemas.
- `repositories/` — concrete implementations of core ports. Depending on the
  chosen ORM, this contains:
  - `{{moduleName}}.orm-entity.ts` — TypeORM entity (persistence-only)
  - `{{moduleName}}.schema.ts` — Mongoose schema/model (persistence-only)
  - `{{moduleName}}.repository.ts` — all ORM implementations + in-memory

## Rules

- Controllers are plain classes — no decorators. The routes factory binds
  HTTP verbs to controller methods.
- Repositories implement the port from `core/ports/`. They map between ORM
  rows and domain entities.
- ORM entities (`orm-entity.ts`, `.schema.ts`) are persistence details — they
  are NOT the domain entity. Keep them in this layer.
